---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import MapStructureDemo from "../../components/MapStructureDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { orMapTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="OR-map" description="Alice removes an observed stockpile while the map retains Bob's concurrent tally update." territory="Structures" sheetTitle="OR-map">
  <article class="register-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro"><p class="territory-label">Structures</p><h1>OR-map</h1><p class="structure-summary">Each hiker has an Eagle Creek stockpile line in their notebook. Alice crosses out the line she saw while Bob records a delivery that she has not seen.</p><LessonIllustration id="structures-or-map" /></header>
    <StructureFacts structure="OR-map" family="CRDT" model="Observed-remove map with nested CRDT values" updates="Change a tally or remove a named entry" merge="Remove what was seen; keep unseen changes made at the same time." delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery" bestFor="Named ledgers where new work must survive deletion" cost="Entry identities, tally state, and a record of removals" />
    <section aria-labelledby="identity-title"><h2 id="identity-title">Cross out only what you have seen</h2><p>In an <dfn><a href="/glossary/#or-map">OR-map</a></dfn>, Alice's crossed-out line applies to the stockpile entry she saw. Bob adds 3 crates to his own copy before he sees her change. His new note was not part of Alice's removal, so the stockpile line remains.</p><TermCallout {...orMapTerm} /><figure><table aria-label="OR-map stockpile race"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Hiker</th><th scope="col">Note</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Alice</th><td>Cross out the 5-crate line she saw</td><td>Her old entry is removed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Bob</th><td>Add 3 crates before he sees Alice's note</td><td>His new note remains</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">All</th><td>Compare notebooks</td><td>Eagle Creek · 8</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption>The tally includes all 8 crates because Bob's new note keeps the line in place.</figcaption></figure></section>
    <MapStructureDemo kind="or-map" title="Keep a new stockpile note" description="Start with 5 crates. Alice crosses out the line she saw while Bob logs 3 more. Compare their notebooks." rule="Crossing out an entry does not remove a new note you have not seen." raceLabel="Race removal against the 3-crate delivery" />
    <section aria-labelledby="modes-title"><h2 id="modes-title">Each line still needs a rule</h2><p>Watershed OR-maps can hold tallies, single answers chosen by time, multiple answers, or lists of text. Each shared notebook uses one of these kinds. The map decides whether a line stays; the kind of answer decides how its changes combine.</p></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Sources:</strong> Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/or_map_kernel.gleam">OR-map kernel</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Implementation:</strong> The demo calls the kernel's tally mode
        through the Gleam toolkit to merge the three clients' stockpile updates.
      </p>
    </section>
    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through map structures"><a href="/structures/lww-map/">Back to LWWMap</a><a href="/structures/maps/">Browse map family</a><a href="/structures/shared-directory/">Continue to SharedDirectory</a></nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
